<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Irish Parliamentary Party</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1882–1922</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Irish Parliamentary Party was the Irish nationalist party in the UK House of Commons that campaigned for Home Rule. Organised under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-stewart-parnell">Charles Stewart Parnell</a>, it held the balance of power in 1885–1886 and again from 1910 under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-redmond">John Redmond</a>, but after the Easter Rising and the conscription crisis it was swept aside by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sinn-fein">Sinn Féin</a> in the general election of 1918.</p></div>
